spoint terrain TEXTURES require SAME-ORIGIN mapspinner (not unpkg): gl-render builds the surface texture by drawImage+getImageData de-shading the photo JPGs (textures/grass|rock|sand|snow). If the SDK is loaded CROSS-ORIGIN (spoint via unpkg), the texture Image taints the canvas -> getImageData throws SecurityError -> texture build silently fails -> FLAT untextured terrain. Two fixes: (1) gl-render now sets img.crossOrigin='anonymous' (tv8 commit 2eb2f08; unpkg serves Access-Control-Allow-Origin:*, so the published SDK textures work cross-origin once 2eb2f08 publishes); (2) spoint reverted its importmap + worker dual-import to SAME-ORIGIN /node_modules/mapspinner (synced from the ../tv8 WORKING TREE) - same-origin needs no crossOrigin AND lets spoint match tv8's exact LOCAL shape (ahead of the published unpkg). To match tv8's exact shape: radius 63600 + reliefScale 0.01 (tv8 demo _planetScale 0.01 = RADIUS 63.71km, WEBGL2_TERRAIN_R_M 63600, reliefScale R/6360000 default); reliefScale 0.05 was 5x = spiky. Consistent node_modules version (render==worker-physics) also fixes collision-under-ground from a version skew. The textures live at the package-ROOT /textures/ (gl-render fetches ../textures/ from src/ via import.meta.url).